# gen_fu_l52_commands_corrigendum.log -- the commands, fixtures and out directories behind every figure in
# gen_fu_l52_irq_entry_bound.log (TB Infra, 2026-09-05). Landing 54.
#
# WHAT THIS CORRECTS. gen_fu_l52_irq_entry_bound.log closes with "Every figure above is produced by the
# command printed above its block", and its blocks print no fixture, no plusargs, no out directory and no
# verdict path. rev59 and the Critic's L-1 both call it: the figures are internally consistent and not
# reproducible from the log. Its bytes are untouched, md5 fe418c61e39bf272f2814ec581a82794, 9116 bytes.
# Everything below is read from the run directories themselves, from each run's run_header.txt and
# verdict.txt, not reconstructed from memory. Fire counts are re-derived here rather than copied.
#
# COUNTING RULE. A UVM run ends with a tally line whose text is UVM_ERROR, a colon and a count, carrying no
# message, and grep -c UVM_ERROR counts it as an error. Counts below match '^UVM_ERROR [^:]'. Two figures move because of it and
# both are error TOTALS, not fire counts: see the quiet block.
#
# THE ONE COMPILE. The log's header line names out_l52c. That build is
#   $ bash dv/auto_dv/tb/gen_tb_local.sh compile <clone>/dv/auto_dv/out_l52c
#   build_sources_sha256 9904576dbd01808d
# but it is NOT the only build the log's figures come from, and the header sentence "THE ONE BUILD EVERY
# FIGURE COMES FROM" is wrong. Five builds appear: out_l49 (2e0d5cbfb591fa07, the committed checker),
# out_l52 (907726226184d9b7, the first fix), out_l52b (028cd081da77bc56, the structural fix),
# out_l52c (9904576dbd01808d, the final build) and out_l52mut (4d318ae1af370965, the mutant).
#
